References: <37A0A965AB353B4D93AE86C2F16FF3825690DA@IRMAIL134.irvine.allergan.com>
Message-ID: <497AEAAF.3020205@elmo.ch>

Pasting the values will create the combinations you want to split by.
I think what you are looking for is something like this.

y <- split(x, paste(x$V2, x$V3))

To be sure that factors do not do weird stuff,
make them characters first:
y <- split(x, paste(as.character(x$V2), as.character(x$V3)))

You can then use lapply/ sapply to process the tables, for example to 
get the means of V4:

sapply(y, function(x) mean(x$V4))

Best regards,

  Andreas

